# Faraday's dev inittab: the release one (common/rootfs-overlay/etc/
# inittab) plus upstream's getty on the board's console tty, which
# build.sh fills in for @TTY@. Upstream's template has no app loop, so
# without this copy the dev image would not restart the app on a lock.
#
# BusyBox init starts `respawn` entries only after every `wait` entry has
# ended, so with the app loop as a `wait` the getty never came. Here the
# loop is a `once` entry that powers off when it ends, and the getty runs
# beside it.
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS
::sysinit:/bin/sh -c 'mkdir -p /run/faraday && chown faraday:faraday /run/faraday && chmod 0700 /run/faraday'
# The kernel log is readable by the app's user, which the release image
# keeps closed: the app reads it with dmesg for the boot report it keeps
# on the stick (faraday/shells/stick/src/bootreport.rs).
::sysinit:/bin/sh -c 'echo 0 > /proc/sys/kernel/dmesg_restrict'
# The app's error output goes to the kernel log, which a laptop shows on
# its screen: a laptop has no serial port to read ttyS0 on. When the app
# ends with anything but a lock, the code is said there too, and the
# machine waits a minute before it powers off, so it can be read. So that a
# machine with no screen and no serial port can say why too, what the kernel
# found is saved as faraday-app-ended.txt on the data partition, at once and
# again before the power-off, with mtools (a Pi kernel has no FAT). Status 76 is Restart on the power sheet: the
# computer restarts at once.
::once:/bin/sh -c 'while :; do /bin/setpriv --nnp /usr/bin/setuidgid faraday /usr/bin/faraday $(cat /etc/faraday/args /run/faraday-screen/args 2>/dev/null) 2>/dev/kmsg; code=$?; [ $code -eq 75 ] || break; done; if [ $code -eq 76 ]; then /sbin/reboot -f; else echo "faraday: the app ended with code $code; power-off in 60 s" > /dev/kmsg; for w in 0 60; do sleep $w; { echo "app ended with code $code"; ls -l /dev/fb* /dev/dri; cat /proc/fb; grep -H . /sys/class/drm/*/status; cat /run/faraday-screen/args; dmesg; } > /run/app-ended.txt 2>&1; MTOOLS_SKIP_CHECK=1 /usr/bin/mcopy -o -i "$(cat /etc/faraday/exchange)" /run/app-ended.txt ::faraday-app-ended.txt 2> /dev/kmsg; done; /sbin/poweroff -f; fi'
@TTY@::respawn:/sbin/getty -L @TTY@ 115200 vt100
